  "live_records": {
    "q-88523": {
      "dom_id": "step-q88523",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Suppose that $A$ and $B$ are two events such that $P(A\\cap B)=\\frac{3}{8}$ and  $P(B)=\\frac{3}{4}.$ What is $P(A|B)?$",
      "worked_solution": "We use the definition of the conditional probability $P(A|B):$\n\n$$\nP(A|B)=\\frac{P(A\\cap B)}{P(B)}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given values, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A|B) & =\\frac{P(A\\cap B)}{P(B)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{3}{8})}{(\\frac{3}{4})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
