    "q-5472": {
      "dom_id": "step-q5472",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Suppose that $A$ and $B$ are two events such that $P(A\\cap B)=\\frac{1}{2}$ and $P(A)=\\frac{2}{3}.$ Find $P(B|A).$",
      "worked_solution": "We use the definition of the conditional probability $P(B|A):$\n\n$$\nP(B|A)=\\frac{P(A\\cap B)}{P(A)}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given values, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(B|A) & =\\frac{P(A\\cap B)}{P(A)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{2})}{(\\frac{2}{3})} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-5472-a",
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\frac{3}{2}",
              "html": "<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"20\" style=\"font-size: 119.6%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mstyle><mjx-mfrac><mjx-frac type=\"d\"><mjx-num><mjx-nstrut type=\"d\"></mjx-nstrut><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c33\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-num><mjx-dbox><mjx-dtable><mjx-line type=\"d\"></mjx-line><mjx-row><mjx-den><mjx-dstrut type=\"d\"></mjx-dstrut><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-den></mjx-row></mjx-dtable></mjx-dbox></mjx-frac></mjx-mfrac></mjx-mstyle></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>"
            },
            {
              "option": "b",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-5472-b",
