    "q-88527": {
      "dom_id": "step-q88527",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Two dice are thrown. Both dice land on the same number. What is the probability that this number is $5?$",
      "worked_solution": "Let us call $F$ the event \"both dice landed on $5$\" and $E$ the event \"both dice landed on the same number.\"\n\nThe required probability is $P(F|E)$, which is given by\n\n$$\nP(F|E)=\\frac{P(F\\cap E)}{P(E)}.\n$$\n\nLet's find $P(E)$ and $P(F\\cap E).$\n\n- There are $6$ possibilities of getting the same number on both dice among the $6\\times 6=36$ possible combinations. So, we have\n\n$$\nP(E)=\\frac{6}{36}=\\frac{1}{6}.\n$$\n\n- There is only one possibility to get $5$ on both dice. So, we have\n\n$$\nP(F\\cap E)=\\frac{1}{36}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, substituting the above into our formula for $P(F|E),$ we get\n\n$$\nP(F|E)=\\frac{(\\frac{1}{36})}{(\\frac{1}{6})}=\\frac{1}{6}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
